{"availability":"available","full":"humanpred/pknca","name":"pknca","description":"An R package is designed to perform all noncompartmental analysis (NCA) calculations for pharmacokinetic (PK) data.","category":"Design","language":"R","stars":86,"forks":32,"created":"2014-12-31T18:20:20Z","updated":"2026-10-09T02:58:48Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"http://humanpred.github.io/pknca/","topics":["cran","nca","noncompartmental-analysis","pharmacokinetics","r"],"demo":"http://humanpred.github.io/pknca/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T08:56:43.439Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T08:56:43.439Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T08:56:43.439Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:39.558Z","stars":86,"forks":32},{"at":"2026-10-09T08:56:43.439Z","stars":86,"forks":32}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The PKNCA R package is designed to perform all noncompartmental analysis (NCA) calculations for pharmacokinetic (PK) data. The package is broadly separated into two parts (calculation and summary) with some additional housekeeping functions.","Along with dense-sampling NCA and its summaries, PKNCA supports:","The primary and secondary goals of the PKNCA package are to 1) only give correct answers to the specific questions being asked and 2) automate as much as possible to simplify the task of the analyst. When automation would leave ambiguity or make a choice that the analyst may have an alternate preference for, it is either not used, is possible to override or raises an error message."],"features":["sparse sampling designs (vignette(\"v04-sparse\"))","units, including automatic conversion to preferred reporting units","imputation of missing or unmeasured data","CDISC-formatted output (as.data.frame(outformat = \"cdisc\"))","bioequivalence assessment (vignette(\"v50-bioequivalence\"))"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/humanpred/pknca/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d12449030e49220ab7e46ed1a4